{
  "schema": "pocol-m1-br16-generator/1",
  "specVersion": "M1 draft 0.6",
  "revision": "R6-06 (annex row B11)",
  "baseline": "FD:L2697-2705 (BR16: 10^4 random messages from a generator seeded with b_i; names from Ethereum, PoCol, anvil and site_* lists with mutations; random kind inside and outside the set; random params; structural envelope mutations; storage_set values near the quota limits). b_i = SHA256('PoColSeed' || be32(i)) (FD:L2522).",
  "label": "The algorithm below is P (the baseline fixes the inputs and the seed family, not the algorithm). It is specified so that a JavaScript BadSite and the Python BridgeRef produce byte-identical message streams; tools/br16_gen.py and tools/br16_gen.cjs implement it, and the runner compares their stream hashes.",
  "seedIndex": 0,
  "count": 10000,
  "prng": "block_k = SHA256(seed || be64(k)) for k = 0, 1, ...; u32() takes the next 4 bytes of the block stream, big-endian; r(n) = u32() mod n.",
  "serializer": "Compact JSON written by the generator itself: integers in decimal; strings with only '\"' -> \\\", '\\\\' -> \\\\\\\\ and code points below 0x20 -> \\u00XX (lowercase hex) escaped; objects as ordered key/value pairs (duplicates allowed, written as given).",
  "algorithm": [
    "for j in 0..count-1:",
    "  if j mod 50 == 49: near-quota storage message: key 'k' x [1,255,256,257][r(4)], value 'a' x [0,1,61439,61440,61441][r(5)], id j+1, kind storage_set, method site_storageSet",
    "  else if r(10) == 0: structural template m = r(12) (see templates), id j+1",
    "  else: id = [0, 4294967295, j+1, j+1, j+1][r(5)]; kind = valid[r(4)] if r(10) < 8 else bad[r(6)];",
    "        method = matrixMethods[kind][r(len)] if kind is valid and r(2) == 0 else names[r(len)];",
    "        if r(4) == 0: method = mutate(method, r(6));",
    "        params = samples[method] if method in samples and r(2) == 0 else [gen(1) for r(4) items]",
    "gen(depth): c = r(8): 0 -> r(1000); 1 -> strs[r(len)]; 2 -> (r(2) == 0); 3 -> null; 4 -> '0x' + 5 x hex8(u32()); 5 -> '0x' + 8 x hex8(u32());",
    "            6 -> depth < 3 ? [gen(depth+1) for r(3) items] : null; 7 -> depth < 3 ? pairs [(keys[r(len)], gen(depth+1)) for r(3) items] : null",
    "mutate(name, m): 0 upper-case ASCII; 1 append ' '; 2 append U+0000; 3 replace the first 'a' by U+0430 (unchanged if none); 4 drop the last character; 5 proto[r(4)]"
  ],
  "templates": [
    "0: the normal text for {id j+1, rpc_read, eth_blockNumber, []} cut to its first floor(len/2) characters",
    "1: payload is an array of two payload objects (BR5)",
    "2: extra outer field \"x\":0",
    "3: extra payload field \"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\"",
    "4: payload without params",
    "5: duplicate key method",
    "6: id written as a string",
    "7: id -1",
    "8: id 4294967296",
    "9: id 1.5",
    "10: params [[[[[[[]]]]]]] (depth 9)",
    "11: eth_call with one string param padded so the text is exactly 65537 bytes"
  ],
  "validKinds": [
    "rpc_read",
    "wallet_req",
    "storage_set",
    "nav"
  ],
